{"id": "EUVD-2026-103049", "enisaUuid": "0edf3a8b-f93c-31be-9957-1afbdd67cf26", "description": "HestiaCP before 1.10.5 contains an authorization bypass vulnerability that allows non-ROOT_USER administrators to perform write actions while impersonating the protected ROOT_USER account. Attackers can log in via the loginas parameter and POST to /add/cron/, because the read-only flag is never checked, causing crond to run their commands as the protected administrator's system account.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:32:00", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/hestiacp/hestiacp/security/advisories/GHSA-vp7q-fjv5-5vg8", "https://github.com/hestiacp/hestiacp/blob/1.10.4/web/add/cron/index.php#L11-L70", "https://github.com/hestiacp/hestiacp/blob/1.10.4/web/inc/policies.php#L3-L14", "https://github.com/hestiacp/hestiacp/commit/1af7e057cd5ad2ea945acba6c9932ea1a1802c24", "https://github.com/hestiacp/hestiacp/releases/tag/1.10.5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/hestiacp-before-1.10.5-protected-admin-bypass-via-cron-job-creation"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8hv6-g9hp-x82m", "CVE-2026-111627"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2a4654a9-b2d1-39bb-b386-de524a8fa24d", "product": {"name": "hestiacp", "vendor": {"name": "hestiacp"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.10.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b95f46df-9906-3a50-968e-1e9200f7fbb2", "vendor": {"name": "hestiacp"}}], "isExploited": false}